# Copy to .env — never commit the real key
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Optional: directory the agent's read-only tools operate in
AGENT_WORKDIR=
# Optional: per-session worktree root for multi-session projects (v2).
# Each session gets AGENT_WORKDIR_ROOT/<sessionId> as its working directory.
AGENT_WORKDIR_ROOT=

# --- GitHub sign-in (A2a) -------------------------------------------------
# OFF unless GITHUB_CLIENT_ID is set. Leave all four blank for ordinary local
# development: identities stay anonymous and every screen behaves as it always
# has. Setting SOME of them fails the boot on purpose — a half-configured auth
# setup would silently run anonymous and look like a bug.
#
# To develop against a real GitHub OAuth app, register a throwaway one with
# callback URL http://localhost:5173/auth/callback (the vite dev server proxies
# /auth through to this server — see poc/client/vite.config.ts) and fill in:
#
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SESSION_SECRET=          # openssl rand -hex 32; changing it signs everyone out
# GITHUB_ALLOWLIST=your-github-login   # comma-separated, case-insensitive,
#                                      # EMPTY ADMITS NOBODY
# OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL=      # optional; see deploy/env.example
